|~ `::elision`, the kind of what a view leaves where it left a part out,
   and the laws declared under it.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence], [QSPRN#elide]. ~|

:elision
  |~~ An elision stands for a part of a value that a budget left out,
      and keeps the way back to it. A reader's context only grows, so
      `elide 4000` cuts a value to a budget, a host cuts so the head of an
      answer past the budget of every answer and the alert of a failure,
      and every part left out gives way to an elision.

      It prints as a map under its tag,
      `::elision{:size 28 :read ~(!| get /trace/0 | subject | drop 2)}`:
      `:size` counts the elements, the entries or the characters it
      stands for, `:read` is the query that, continued from the answer,
      reads the part left out, `~()` for the answer itself, and `:head`
      holds the first characters of the text of a string, a doc or a
      quote, or of the print a kind gives a part. The rest of a map stands
      under the key `:"…"`, `{:a 1 :"…" ::elision{:size 7 :read ~(drop 1)}}`,
      and the elision of a rest stands last in a vector. A failure the
      host prints is an alert, each subject it passed given way to an
      elision where the elision prints shorter, and past a budget its
      trace keeps its first frames and an elision of the rest, and its
      facts give way, each under its name.
      ::link~(::any/elide | doc) ::link~(::qlang/hosts | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts
        |~~ The size of the part left out, the query that reads it and the
            head of its text.
        ~~|
        ::map
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ An elision is the map of a part left out, its size, the query
            that reads it and the head of its text, which `elide` writes,
            `x | elide 20`.
        ~~|
    | proves :measuresWhatItLeftOut
        |~~ An elision holds the size of what it left out. ~~|
        ~({:s "a long line of text to leave out, which runs on long enough that its elision prints shorter than it"}
          | elide 20 | get /s | get /size | eq 99)

